bqI(){return A.a1U(!0,"Svg",A.b([A.zh(new A.aU1(),"https://github.com/adario/rasterizer_flutter/blob/main/flame_rasterizer/example/lib/stories/svg/svg_renderers_example.dart","    The same SVG drawn many times, by flame_rasterizer or by flame_svg: one in\n    the centre, and a ring of 10 to 500 around it, all rotating.\n\n    GPU (mesh), GPU (atlas) and Canvas draw with flame_rasterizer, through one\n    of rasterizer_gpu's renderers. The mesh renderer, the default, imports\n    each SVG once into triangles that stay on the GPU. The atlas renderer\n    rasterizes the SVGs into an atlas each frame. The canvas renderer draws\n    their paths into Flutter's canvas. A GPU entry is inactive where its\n    renderer can't run, as on the web. Flame SVG draws with flame_svg, which\n    caches each SVG as an image per size on screen. Zoomed in,\n    flame_rasterizer stays sharp, while flame_svg makes new images or scales\n    the ones it cached, as the cache knobs say.\n\n    The other knobs pick the SVG and the SVG number, fade the ring's SVGs,\n    zoom the camera and change the rotation's speed. Only a new renderer makes\n    a new game, which turns on from the same angles. The bar under the game\n    shows the renderer, the frame times and the renderer's own numbers.\n\n    flame_rasterizer doesn't support clip paths, so alien, invader_1,\n    invader_2, recycle, recycle_merge, setup and setup_merge draw unclipped\n    with it.\n  ","Svg Renderers"),A.zh(new A.aU2(),"https://github.com/adario/rasterizer_flutter/blob/main/flame_rasterizer/example/lib/stories/svg/collidable_svgs_example.dart","    SVGs picked at random move and spin, like the birds of Flame's animated\n    collision example. Their hitboxes follow the contours of their paths:\n    they're flame_rasterizer's SvgHitbox, whatever draws the SVGs. Two SVGs\n    that collide swap their velocities, and an SVG that hits a wall turns\n    back.\n\n    The knobs pick the renderer and the SVG number, zoom the camera and change\n    the SVGs' speed. With Flame SVG, the cache knobs set flame_svg's cache.\n    Only a new renderer or cache makes a new game. A new renderer's game goes\n    on with the same SVGs, from where they were. The bar under the game shows\n    the renderer, the frame times, the renderer's own numbers and the\n    collisions so far.\n\n    Based on flame_path_shapes' CollidableSvgPathsExample.\n  ","Collidable Svgs")],t.Jw))},
